<title>BELGIUM: EU vets acquisition of Finnish Chemicals.</title>
<headline>EU vets acquisition of Finnish Chemicals.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Thursday it had started a routine review of the planned takeover of Finnish Chemicals by Prudential Nominees Ltd and HSBC Equity Ltd.</p>
<p>Prudential Nominees, controlled by Prudential Corporation, is a supplier of life insurances and HSBC Equity is active in banking and financial services.</p>
<p>Finnish Chemicals makes and supplies pulping and bleaching chemicals for pulp and paper industries.</p>
<p>The Commission, which vets corporate deals to see whether they may harm competition in the EU, has one month to complete its investigation. If it has doubts about approving a deal, it may start a second stage, four-month investigation. Most deals are cleared after one month.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
